# Copy to .env.local for `next dev`. On Vercel, set the same names for Production.
# With none of these set, `next dev` logs the signup and plays the confirmation
# animation without contacting a list. A Vercel production deployment refuses
# that path and does not tell the reader they were subscribed.

# The Agentic Rewind — Resend Contacts.
# Provide the API key plus a segment id (current Contacts API) or a legacy audience id.
# Segment wins when both are set. A 409 from Resend means the address is already
# a contact; the adapter then adds that contact to the segment.
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_AGENTIC_SEGMENT_ID=
# RESEND_AGENTIC_AUDIENCE_ID=

# The React Native Rewind — MailerLite.
# This is the list the live site's domain is authorized to send from.
# Optional group id limits the subscriber to one MailerLite group.
# Optional status: active, unconfirmed, unsubscribed, bounced, junk.
# Leave status unset to use MailerLite's default. Set unconfirmed if that
# account still requires its own confirmation email.
MAILERLITE_API_KEY=
# MAILERLITE_GROUP_ID=
# MAILERLITE_STATUS=

# Optional Strapi subscriber write. Used only when MAILERLITE_API_KEY is unset.
# Strapi Cloud for the React Native Rewind site is the content CMS
# (https://studio.thereactnativerewind.com). No public subscriber collection
# was found there, so confirm the path before relying on this.
# STRAPI_URL=https://studio.thereactnativerewind.com
# STRAPI_API_TOKEN=
# STRAPI_SUBSCRIBERS_PATH=/api/subscribers
# STRAPI_EMAIL_FIELD=email
